## Context

Ticket 1375 (PR #2054, parked by the author's ruling on 2026-10-30, raid
80974c) tried to fix the seat scrub (`scripts/gaze_seat.py` `SCRUB_PATTERNS`,
`scrub`) by patching regexes. Six review rounds of gaze with an OpenAI seat
(review rv-20261030-pr-2054-cfb1 on notes) each closed one leak and opened a
neighbouring one:

1. value regex: backslash, unterminated, comma-tail values leaked; newline crossing ate parsed answer fields;
2. a quote of the other kind ended a quoted value;
3. a doubly-escaped inner quote ended it;
4. (opener regex + linear scanner) the rest of the line was consumed, so a second secret on a line was skipped;
5. the Bearer pattern, running first, ate a closing quote the scanner needs;
6. key=value running first takes only `Bearer` from `X-Auth-Token: Bearer FAKEopaque` and leaves the token.

Diagnosis: the patterns run one after another over text the previous one
rewrote, so each pattern's correctness depends on the order and output of the
others. The problem is not one regex but the sequential design.

The parked branch `t1375-scrub-gaze-close` (head 6ff80a32) holds the shape
corpus as tests and the parts that held: the answer-text scrub in
`gaze_close.py` (seat bodies quoted into a gaze answer reach
`refs/notes/review` verbatim), the no-line-crossing rule, and the
`skills/gaze/references/panel.md` boundary.

## Ruling (author, 2026-10-30)

Regex filtering rarely works, and recurring friction weighs more than a
one-time build: no scanner, no LLM judge (latency, outages, false
positives, a pending backlog every close). Instead remove the channel that
needs filtering and keep main's crude scrub, whose failure mode
(over-redaction) costs a few words and never blocks.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The seat failure line written to notes (`<name>.md.status`, the
  `stderr:` part of a failed outcome) carries only fields the harness owns:
  exit code, timed out or not, duration, door, model, report present or not.
  No CLI stderr text reaches notes; the raw stderr stays in the seat's local
  `.log`. A test plants a fake secret in a stub's stderr and finds it in no
  status line or note.
- [ ] `scrub()` keeps origin/main's key=value value matching (`\S+`) and gains
  only the key-side fixes that never touched value ends: a backslash-escaped
  JSON key (`{\"access_token\": ...}`), a spaced `Account ID:` label, and no
  match across a newline (so parsed answer fields survive). One red-first test
  each.
- [ ] `gaze_close.py` scrubs the answer's free text with that `scrub()` (the
  held part of PR #2054), with the parsed fields byte-identical.
- [ ] PR #2054 is closed unmerged, pointing here.

Not in scope by ruling: an error class read from CLI output (vendor formats
change; add later only if debugging hurts), a grammar on seat reports.

## Plan (raid 0da24b: Imagine, Blind-Spot, feasibility)

Premise holds. Chain: `seat_clock.py:102` CLI stderr → `<out>.log` →
`gaze_seat.py` `stderr_excerpt()` → `failed()` appends `; stderr: …` →
`main()` writes `<name>.md.status` → the gaze orchestrator copies the cause
into the answer's `ran:` line (`panel.md:50`) → `gaze_close.py` → notes. No
script parses the `stderr:` text (wait-roster, seat_clock plan-check and
identities, review_notes SEAT_LINE checked).

Actions:
1. Red first: a stub seat writes a canary secret to stderr and fails; assert
   the canary is absent from `<name>.md.status` and the printed line, and
   present in `<out>.log` (positive control). Same for a seat whose report is
   a `NOT-RUN:` refusal quoting a canary: `failed()` now quotes it.
2. `failed()` keeps run_seat's owned outcome (`exit N`, `timed out after Ns`,
   `empty output, Ns`, `failed to start`) and appends door and model; no stderr
   excerpt, and a refusal is the fixed `seat refused (NOT-RUN)`. Delete
   `stderr_excerpt` and `STDERR_EXCERPT_CHARS`. Rewrite the tests that assert
   the old strings (`tests/test_gaze_seat.py` around 172, 220, 284-288, 661-663,
   722, 730-765). Update `skills/gaze/references/panel.md:50`.
3. Key-side scrub edit on origin/main's pattern only:
   `…account[ _-]?id)(?:\\?["'])?[ \t]*[:=][ \t]*\S+` (escaped JSON key,
   spaced label, no newline crossing); value stays `\S+`. Red tests: escaped
   key, `Account ID: <uuid>`, `access_token:\nreview plan: x` untouched,
   `session id: <uuid>` survives.
4. Port the `gaze_close.py` answer scrub from `origin/t1375-scrub-gaze-close`
   (head 6ff80a32) with its canary test; parsed fields byte-identical. Do not
   port its value-end scanner or its later scrub tests.
5. After merge: close PR #2054 with a comment pointing here; the parked
   worktree `t1375-1259116-31958` is then removed by roar.

Feasibility: PASS. No file overlap with 1379.
